      "movesets": [
        {
          "name": "Physical Wallbreaker",
          "pokemon": "Zeraora",
          "shiny": false,
          "gender": "DC",
          "levels": [],
          "description": "<p>Choice Band Zeraora is a fearsome wallbreaker on Electric teams thanks to its incredible Speed stat and respectable Attack. Close Combat threatens foes like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/blissey/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Blissey</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/ferrothorn/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Ferrothorn</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/goodra-hisui/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Goodra</a> that try to wall Zeraora or its teammates, while Knock Off scares off Ghost- and Psychic-types like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/sinistcha/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Sinistcha</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/slowking-galar/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Galarian Slowking</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/jirachi/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Jirachi</a>. Play Rough hits Dragon- and Fighting-types like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/altaria-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Altaria</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/hydreigon/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hydreigon</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gallade-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Gallade</a> for massive damage. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/tapu-koko/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Tapu Koko</a> complements Zeraora by providing Electric Terrain to amp up Plasma Fists, notably allowing Zeraora to OHKO <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/diancie-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Diancie</a> with the power boost while hitting Dark-, Dragon-, and Ground-types like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/sableye-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Sableye</a>, Mega Altaria, and the <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/landorus/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Landorus</a> formes with its strong Dazzling Gleam and Hidden Power Ice. Tapu Koko appreciates Zeraora dispatching specially defensive walls like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/chansey/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Chansey</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/muk-alola/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Alolan Muk</a>, and Hisuian Goodra with its strong Plasma Fists and Close Combat. Both <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/rotom-wash/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Rotom-W</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/zapdos/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Zapdos</a> are great teammates by virtue of their Ground immunity; Rotom-W can pivot Zeraora in on the aforementioned walls, wash away Ground-types with Hydro Pump, and remove entry hazards with Defog, while Zapdos greatly appreciates said walls being broken down and demolishes Grass-types like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/venusaur-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Venusaur</a> in return. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/iron-hands/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Iron Hands</a> provides a defensive sponge against Choice Scarf users such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/arcanine-hisui/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Arcanine</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/kleavor/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Kleavor</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gholdengo/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Gholdengo</a> and provides entry points thanks to its slow Volt Switch. After a Nasty Plot, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/raichu-alola/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Alolan Raichu</a> can deal with troubling Poison- and Ground-types like Mega Venusaur, Water Absorb <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/clodsire/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Clodsire</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/hippowdon/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hippowdon</a> thanks to its strong Z-Psyshock and Grass Knot, greatly aiding Zeraora's wallbreaking efforts.</p>",
